# GitHub Copilot Agent Mode — Build a Production-Grade JIRA Test Case Generation Agent on Azure AKS

## Role

Act as a Principal AI Architect, senior Node.js/TypeScript developer, Azure cloud architect, MCP integration engineer and Kubernetes specialist.

Implement a complete, production-oriented application in the current GitHub repository. Do not stop at architecture descriptions or pseudocode. Create the source code, tests, database migrations, Dockerfiles, Helm charts, CI/CD workflows and deployment documentation.

Inspect the existing repository before making changes. Preserve useful existing code and conventions. If a component cannot be verified against the available SDK or service, implement a clean adapter interface and mock rather than inventing APIs.

## 1. Business requirement

Build a supervised AI agent that:

1. Accepts a JIRA user story key.
2. Authenticates and authorizes the requesting user.
3. Reads the story description and acceptance criteria through an existing remote MCP server.
4. Retrieves relevant context from Confluence, Figma, existing test cases and enterprise knowledge sources through MCP.
5. Analyzes acceptance criteria and identifies missing requirements and ambiguities.
6. Generates high-quality manual test cases using Claude Opus through Azure AI Foundry.
7. Validates the generated cases and checks acceptance-criteria coverage and duplication.
8. Saves test cases as drafts.
9. Allows a QA reviewer to approve, reject, edit or request regeneration.
10. Publishes approved test cases through a configured JIRA or test-management integration.
11. Records audit events, workflow status, errors, model usage and quality metrics.

**Mandatory rule:** Generated test cases must remain drafts until an authorized human approves them. The LLM must never approve its own output or directly execute privileged publishing operations.

